# A zero-width rule whose action leaves its own guard true would return
# the same token forever (the generated lexer hung on any input).
# error: lexer_zero_width_stuck.grammar:13:1:
# error: after its actions its guards still hold
@lexer
state
    m = 1
tokens
    t
    word
    eof
    err
@ m                                         → t, {m = 1}
[a-z]+                                      → word
.                                           → err

@parser
top! = (T | WORD)*                          → (top ...1)
